			<div class="content" id="post-content-2566947">
									

<p>I agree that the ending came a bit out of nowhere - it might have made more sense to commit fully to the character work, as that was the stronger part of the skip.</p>
<p>I found the early going to be very confusing, and I think it could be rewritten more clearly. The Containment Procedures (not &quot;Special&quot; - is that deliberate?) felt imprecise - in particular the phrase &quot;personnel tasked with containment&quot;, as those people don't really contain so much as read emails.</p>
<p>&quot;incorporeal entity of consciousness&quot; would be more meaningful as &quot;incorporeal consciousness&quot; or &quot;non-localised consciousness&quot;, I think. &quot;periods of unconsciousness between the current and target host&quot; is also unclear - you mean when they're both asleep, I presume.</p>
<p>The discovery paragraph is quite difficult to believe. Why would the Foundation have noted the mental health forum posts as suggesting any anomalous activity - that level of detailed surveillance breaks my suspension of disbelief. And the idea of reports of those types of behaviours (a) being made in a way (across the entire human population) that is able to be tracked by the Foundation at all; and (b) being sufficiently consistent that the Foundation could determine that they were related - likewise, I don't buy it.</p>
<p>Finally, you have two paragraphs dealing with the set-up of the email address (one before the forum excerpt and one after). The second one is somewhat easier to understand - you'd be better off deleting the first.</p>

							</div>

								
					
